{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שלום", :translit "shalom", :gloss "peace"} {:he "אותיות לשמו", :translit "otiot lishmo", :gloss "the letters of His name"} {:he "ששמו שלום", :translit "she-shmo shalom", :gloss "for His name is Peace"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The word שלום is identical in letters to the divine name שלום."}], :frame {:text "The name 'Shalom' is identified as a divine name: Judges 6:24 records Gideon's altar named 'Hashem Shalom,' and Shabbat 10b states that Shalom is one of God's names. The Sifrei on Numbers 6:26 likewise associates the priestly blessing of peace with the divine name.", :sources ["Judges 6:24" "Shabbat 10b" "Sifrei Numbers 6:26"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והשבתי חיה רעה", :translit "v'hashavti chayah ra'ah", :gloss "and I will cause harmful beasts to cease"} {:he "אלו ד' מלכיות", :translit "elu arba malkhiyot", :gloss "these are the four kingdoms"} {:he "בבל מדי יון אדום", :translit "bavel madai yavan edom", :gloss "Babylon Media Greece Edom"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "והשבתי חיה רעה", :b "בבל מדי יון אדום"}], :frame {:text "The scheme of four successive empires — Babylon, Media, Greece, and Edom (Rome) — that dominate Israel derives from Daniel's vision of four beasts (Daniel 7:3–7) and is enumerated in terms of these four kingdoms in the exposition of Leviticus 26 in Midrash Rabbah.", :sources ["Daniel 7:3–7" "Leviticus Rabbah 13:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The word שלום is identical in letters to the divine name שלום.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "והשבתי חיה רעה", :a-value 1021, :b "בבל מדי יון אדום", :b-value 205, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:56.692948641Z", :model "glm-5.2"}